-- title:
--   Weight-2 cusp forms on Γ₁(M) as q-expansions of differentials
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $M$, a ring homomorphism $\iota_0 : \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathbb C$ from the algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$, and a cusp form $f$ of weight $2$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(M)$, and assume that every coefficient of the power series `UpperHalfPlane.qExpansion 1 f` (the $q$-expansion of $f$ with width $1$) lies in the image of $\iota_0$. Let $F =$ `x1FunctionFieldBar M` be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ M` $\subseteq \mathbb Q((q))$, and let `diffQExp` $: \Omega_{F/\overline{\mathbb Q}} \to \overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ be the $F$-linear map obtained by lifting to Kähler differentials the derivation `qEuler` of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ restricted along the inclusion of $F$. The assertion is that there exists $\omega \in \Omega_{F/\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ whose image under `diffQExp`, after applying $\iota_0$ to every Laurent coefficient, equals the Laurent series over $\mathbb C$ attached to the power series `UpperHalfPlane.qExpansion 1 f`.
--
--   This realises a weight-$2$ cusp form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ with coefficients algebraic over $\mathbb Q$ as the $q$-expansion of a Kähler differential on the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(M)$ base changed to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, one half of the classical identification of $S_2(\Gamma_1(M))$ with the differentials of $X_1(M)$. It feeds the construction of the isomorphism between the regular differentials of $X_1(M)_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}$, tensored up, and weight-$2$ cusp forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_coeffMap_diffQExp_x1FunctionFieldBar_eq_qExpansion.lean

